\par\par \b \uc2 MOF:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  To Continue Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  On Thurs If Necessary-Kyodo\b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 16:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Ministry official said the government will continue to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb the yen's rise on Thursday if necessary, Kyodo News reported Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted their first \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in over six years on Wednesday in a surprising move that reflected their fears that the country's economic recovery could slow down.\par \par \uc2 The yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , implemented several times both in Tokyo and overseas trading, helped the U.S. dollar rise back above the Y85 line from the upper Y82 yen. Market participants said the emergency step may have only a limited effect, however.\par \par \uc2 The focus is now shifting to whether the Bank of Japan could take additional easing measures in its monetary policy and help weaken the yen in line with the government step.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Naoto Kan said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had some positive effects in reining in the yen's recent sharp rise against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "As we have said before, rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations are undesirable and we will take decisive steps when needed," Kan told reporters. "Today the fluctuations reached a stage where we could not leave them uncontrolled. So we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Another Finance Ministry official said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has "implemented an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of considerable scale," with some market sources estimating the amount of yen the authorities sold came to around Y1 trillion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted unilaterally, Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said, sparking doubts among market players about its effectiveness.\par \par \uc2 The move by the Japanese monetary authorities came after Kan was reelected as president of the Democratic Party of Japan on Tuesday, beating ruling party heavyweight and sole challenger Ichiro Ozawa.\par \par \uc2 Fumito Akiyama, fund manager at \uc2 Sparx Asset Management Co\uc2 ., said the Japanese government's move will not change the current situation significantly.\par \par \uc2 "The timing (of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) was interesting to some extent," Akiyama said. As the gap remains between Japan and the United States over their inflation expectations, however, "the yen will rise (against the dollar) in the medium and long term," he said, adding it is "natural" for the yen to be bought given that the Japanese economy is experiencing deflation.\par \par \uc2 He also said it is unlikely the United States will join Tokyo's attempt to weaken the yen and strengthen the dollar as President Barack Obama has expressed his intention to accelerate U.S. exports.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Treasury Department refrained from commenting on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Washington is normally seen as negative about artificial moves in financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Noda said Japan stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market while closely communicating with authorities in other major economies, but declined to reveal their reactions.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on March 16, 2004. Tokyo used more than Y35 trillion in the 15 months through the same month to avert the yen's sharp advance against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2900 [ 09-15-10 1024ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020100915e69f0009g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
