\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Guaranteed Buyer For Treasurys...\b0\par\par\uc2 1,051 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 19:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1729 GMT [Dow Jones] Today the US Treasury got a gift: a future guaranteed buyer of at least $300 billion more in bonds, says ZeroHedge about yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issues debt, raises Yen, uses Yen to buy Dollars, uses Dollars to buy Treasuries, completing the ponzi loop whereby it has just added to its debt, using the proceeds to fund America's endless credit fueled spending spree." (darlene.ross@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.zerohedge.com/article/observations-how-much-capacity-intervention-does-boj-has-and-whether-intervention-will-be-st?utm_source=feedburner&utm_medium=feed&utm_campaign=Feed%3A+zerohedge%2Ffeed+%28zero+hedge+-+on+a+long+enough+timeline%2C+the+survival+rate+for+everyone+drops+to+zero%29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.zerohedge.com/article/observations-how-much-capacity-\b  \highlight22intervention\b0 \highlight22 -does-boj-has-and-whether-\b  \highlight22intervention\b0 \highlight22 -will-be-st?utm_source=feedburner&utm_medium=feed&utm_campaign=Feed%3A+zerohedge%2Ffeed+%28zero+hedge+-+on+a+long+enough+timeline%2C+the+survival+rate+for+everyone+drops+to+zero%29}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 1705 GMT [Dow Jones] Brazilian steelmaker CSN (SID, CSNA3.BR) has received nearly $7 billion in orders for its perpetual bond offer, set to price later Wednesday, according to a person familiar with the matter. Size of the deal hasn't been announced but market participants expecting $1 billion sale. Yield also likely to come in at the low end of the guidance for 7%-7.25%, the person said. (kejal.vyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1702 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Cliffs Natural Resources\uc2  $1B (upsized from $750 mln) 2-part bond offer has launched with a $500 mln 10-yr tranche at 210 bps over Tsys and a $500 mln 30-yr tranche at 250 bps over, according to a person familiar with the deal, with each tranche coming 5 bps tighter than initial price guidance. Via BAML and JPM Morgan. Proceeds will be used to repay credit revolver borrowings and for general corporate purposes. (michael.aneiro@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1657 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 CoreLogic\uc2  economist says the overall housing picture looks similar to prices back in November 2009, when housing was on a decline. \uc2 CoreLogic\uc2  home price index was flat for July, with no change compared to July 2009, the first time in 5 months that no gains were reported. "The majority of states experienced price declines, and these are spreading across more geographies relative to a few months ago," said economist Mark Fleming. (prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 1648 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys maturing in five years or less are likely to be the biggest winners as the preferred place for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to park its dollar proceeds from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Speculation \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take more actions to curb yen's gains spurs some investors to buy short-dated notes and sell long-dated Treasurys, in a trade known as steepening of the curve. The benchmark yield curve, the yield spread of 2yr/10-yr notes, steepens to 221 bp from 216 bp Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1646 GMT [Dow Jones] Mexico's peso shook off opening weakness and rose vs the dollar thanks to U.S. stock gains and a stronger euro. USD/MXN recently quoted in Mexico City at 12.7765 compared with 12.8265 at Tuesday's close. With dollar put options exercisable for a third straight day, banks could sell dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although they held off Monday and Tuesday in a sign further appreciation is expected. The Bank of Mexico sells $600 million a month in put options, which can be exercised when the peso is stronger than its 20-day average. The peso could move toward 12.65 in the near term, said a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader, although "at the first bad news the rate would shoot back up." (anthony.harrup@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1644 GMT [Dow Jones] Brazilian steelmaker CSN (SID, CSNA3.BR), likely to price $1 billion in a perpetual bond offer later Wednesday, according to people close to the transaction. Market watchers looking for bonds to yield around 7%. BofAML, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 , Deutsche and \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  are managing the transaction.(kejal.vyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1622 GMT [Dow Jones] Three auto ABS price: \uc2 BMW\uc2  with $1B, \uc2 AmeriCredit\uc2  $850M and Nissan $1.3B. All were priced over interpolated swaps or EDSF with their largest tranches yielding under 1%. (repeats, adds EDSF as benchmark.)\par \par \uc2 (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1613 GMT [Dow Jones] Three auto ABS price: \uc2 BMW\uc2  with $1B, \uc2 AmeriCredit\uc2  $850M and Nissan $1.3B. All were priced over interpolated swaps with their largest tranches yielding under 1%. (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1613 GMT [Dow Jones] Nearest 1-yr calendar spread is substantially tighter in Eurodollar futures compared to late last week, signaling market fears of a slowing economy and expectations for short-term rates to stay very low for a long time. Dec 2011 contract recently priced in a rate only 41.5 BP above the rate priced into the Dec 2010 contract. Same spread at 42.5 BP Tues, 48.5 BP Mon, and 52 BP Fri. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1551 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by USD/JPY \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options were lower in NY Wed from Tokyo after the dollar leaped against the yen following the \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimated Y1 trillion direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One-month at-the-money USD/JPY options implied volatilities were at 11.80%/12.50%, from 12.45%/13.15% in Tokyo and from 11.85%/12.55% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/USD implied vols were at 10.55%/11.55%, from 10.65%/11.65% in Tokyo and from 10.50%/11.50% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/JPY implied vols were at 13.40%/15.40% from 13.55%/15.55% in Tokyo and from 12.80%/14.80% in NY Tue. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1552 GMT [Dow Jones] The truth is that a very large percentage of Americans consumers is either incredibly scared or totally broke or both, says the Business Insider, with 20 signs the consumer is tapped out. (darlene.ross@dowjones.com)({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.businessinsider.com/20-signs-the-american-consumer-is-completely-and-totally-tapped-out-2010-9?utm_source=feedburner&utm_medium=feed&utm_campaign=Feed%3A+TheMoneyGame+%28The+Money+Game%29#ixzz0zc7QMgQH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.businessinsider.com/20-signs-the-american-consumer-is-completely-and-totally-tapped-out-2010-9?utm_source=feedburner&utm_medium=feed&utm_campaign=Feed%3A+TheMoneyGame+%28The+Money+Game%29#ixzz0zc7QMgQH}}}\uc2 ) [ 09-15-10 1342ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f000cw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
