wing economy and expectations for short-term rates to stay very low for a long time. Dec 2011 contract recently priced in a rate only 41.5 BP above the rate priced into the Dec 2010 contract. Same spread at 42.5 BP Tues, 48.5 BP Mon, and 52 BP Fri. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1551 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by USD/JPY \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options were lower in NY Wed from Tokyo after the dollar leaped against the yen following the \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimated Y1 trillion direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One-month at-the-money USD/JPY options implied volatilities were at 11.80%/12.50%, from 12.45%/13.15% in Tokyo and from 11.85%/12.55% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/USD implied vols were at 10.55%/11.55%, from 10.65%/11.65% in Tokyo and from 10.50%/11.50% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/JPY implied vols were at 13.40%/15.40% from 13.55%/15.55% in Tokyo and from 12.80%/14.80% in NY Tue. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1552 GMT [Dow Jones] The truth is that a very large percentage of Americans consumers is either incredibly scared or totally broke or both, says the Business Insider, with 20 signs the consumer is tapped out. (darlene.ross@dowjones.com)({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.businessinsider.com/20-signs-the-american-consumer-is-completely-and-totally-tapped-out-2010-9?utm_source=feedburner&utm_medium=feed&utm_campaign=Feed%3A+TheMoneyGame+%28The+Money+Game%29#ixzz0zc7QMgQH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.businessinsider.com/20-signs-the-american-consumer-is-completely-and-totally-tapped-out-2010-9?utm_source=feedburner&utm_medium=feed&utm_campaign=Feed%3A+TheMoneyGame+%28The+Money+Game%29#ixzz0zc7QMgQH}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 1532 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 AmeriCredit\uc2  Auto Receivables Trust's $850M ABS, which was increased from $700M, has launched according to a person familiar with the