\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Shortest Treasurys Winners On  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,033 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 18:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1648 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys maturing in five years or less are likely to be the biggest winners as the preferred place for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to park its dollar proceeds from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Speculation \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could take more actions to curb yen's gains spurs some investors to buy short-dated notes and sell long-dated Treasurys, in a trade known as steepening of the curve. The benchmark yield curve, the yield spread of 2yr/10-yr notes, steepens to 221 bp from 216 bp Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1646 GMT [Dow Jones] Mexico's peso shook off opening weakness and rose vs the dollar thanks to U.S. stock gains and a stronger euro. USD/MXN recently quoted in Mexico City at 12.7765 compared with 12.8265 at Tuesday's close. With dollar put options exercisable for a third straight day, banks could sell dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although they held off Monday and Tuesday in a sign further appreciation is expected. The Bank of Mexico sells $600 million a month in put options, which can be exercised when the peso is stronger than its 20-day average. The peso could move toward 12.65 in the near term, said a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader, although "at the first bad news the rate would shoot back up." (anthony.harrup@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1644 GMT [Dow Jones] Brazilian steelmaker CSN (SID, CSNA3.BR), likely to price $1 billion in a perpetual bond offer later Wednesday, according to people close to the transaction. Market watchers looking for bonds to yield around 7%. BofAML, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 , Deutsche and \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  are managing the transaction.(kejal.vyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1622 GMT [Dow Jones] Three auto ABS price: \uc2 BMW\uc2  with $1B, \uc2 AmeriCredit\uc2  $850M and Nissan $1.3B. All were priced over interpolated swaps or EDSF with their largest tranches yielding under 1%. (repeats, adds EDSF as benchmark.)\par \par \uc2 (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1613 GMT [Dow Jones] Three auto ABS price: \uc2 BMW\uc2  with $1B, \uc2 AmeriCredit\uc2  $850M and Nissan $1.3B. All were priced over interpolated swaps with their largest tranches yielding under 1%. (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1613 GMT [Dow Jones] Nearest 1-yr calendar spread is substantially tighter in Eurodollar futures compared to late last week, signaling market fears of a slowing economy and expectations for short-term rates to stay very low for a long time. Dec 2011 contract recently priced in a rate only 41.5 BP above the rate priced into the Dec 2010 contract. Same spread at 42.5 BP Tues, 48.5 BP Mon, and 52 BP Fri. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1551 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by USD/JPY \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options were lower in NY Wed from Tokyo after the dollar leaped against the yen following the \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimated Y1 trillion direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One-month at-the-money USD/JPY options implied volatilities were at 11.80%/12.50%, from 12.45%/13.15% in Tokyo and from 11.85%/12.55% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/USD implied vols were at 10.55%/11.55%, from 10.65%/11.65% in Tokyo and from 10.50%/11.50% Tue in NY. One-month EUR/JPY implied vols were at 13.40%/15.40% from 13.55%/15.55% in Tokyo and from 12.80%/14.80% in NY Tue. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1552 GMT [Dow Jones] The truth is that a very large percentage of Americans consumers is either incredibly scared or totally broke or both, says the Business Insider, with 20 signs the consumer is tapped out. (darlene.ross@dowjones.com)({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.businessinsider.com/20-signs-the-american-consumer-is-completely-and-totally-tapped-out-2010-9?utm_source=feedburner&utm_medium=feed&utm_campaign=Feed%3A+TheMoneyGame+%28The+Money+Game%29#ixzz0zc7QMgQH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.businessinsider.com/20-signs-the-american-consumer-is-completely-and-totally-tapped-out-2010-9?utm_source=feedburner&utm_medium=feed&utm_campaign=Feed%3A+TheMoneyGame+%28The+Money+Game%29#ixzz0zc7QMgQH}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 1532 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 AmeriCredit\uc2  Auto Receivables Trust's $850M ABS, which was increased from $700M, has launched according to a person familiar with the matter. Joint lead managers on the bond, scheduled to price later Wed, are Barc, \uc2 UBS\uc2  and \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2 . Price guidance is also out: the largest tranche valued at $281M, has launched at 35 bps over over EDSF, a benchmark. Price guidance was in the range of 37 to 40 bps over EDSF. (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1522 GMT [Dow Jones] Former Fed chief Alan Greenspan got a chance to air his views at the Council on Foreign Relations today. The man who spent large stretches of his professional life in public service, and who then was handsomely paid to talk about the insights he gained during that time once out of office, continues to see government as one of the economy's problems. "We have to find a way to simmer down the extent of activism that is going on" with government stimulus spending "and allow the economy to heal" itself, he says. At this point, "we'd probably be better off doing less than more" because "you'd be far better off to allow the normal market forces to operate here," Greenspan said. (michael.derby@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1516 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys maturing in 10 yrs or less are gaining after Fed buys 3- to 7-yr sector. Fed bought $3.89B in notes maturing between Sept 2014 and June 2016. The long bond is the only maturity trading lower but it has pared a big chunk of early losses. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1514 GMT [Dow Jones] Repeat & correct: No evidence of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in U.S. market in the face of emerging scuttle that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already acted in N.Y. trading hours, said Hidetoshi Yanagihara, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in New York. Investors are looking for follow-up to roughly Y1 trillion of yen-selling in Asia and Europe so far. (Corrects to fix spelling of firm name in headline at 1505 GMT) (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com) [ 09-15-10 1250ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f000cm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
