ons today. The man who spent large stretches of his professional life in public service, and who then was handsomely paid to talk about the insights he gained during that time once out of office, continues to see government as one of the economy's problems. "We have to find a way to simmer down the extent of activism that is going on" with government stimulus spending "and allow the economy to heal" itself, he says. At this point, "we'd probably be better off doing less than more" because "you'd be far better off to allow the normal market forces to operate here," Greenspan said. (michael.derby@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1516 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys maturing in 10 yrs or less are gaining after Fed buys 3- to 7-yr sector. Fed bought $3.89B in notes maturing between Sept 2014 and June 2016. The long bond is the only maturity trading lower but it has pared a big chunk of early losses. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1514 GMT [Dow Jones] Repeat & correct: No evidence of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in U.S. market in the face of emerging scuttle that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already acted in N.Y. trading hours, said Hidetoshi Yanagihara, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in New York. Investors are looking for follow-up to roughly Y1 trillion of yen-selling in Asia and Europe so far. (Corrects to fix spelling of firm name in headline at 1505 GMT) (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1509 GMT [Dow Jones] Fed buys $3.89B in nine Treasurys notes with maturities spanning between Sept. 30, 2014 and June 30, 2016. Dealers submit $16.628 billion bids. The Fed started small-scale buying in Treasurys last month, using proceeds from its MBS paydowns as a way to push down long-term interest rates to support a slowing economy. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1505 GMT [Dow Jones] No evidence of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in U.S. market in the face of emerging scuttle that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already acted in N.Y. trading hours, said Hidetoshi Yanagihara, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in New York. Investors are looking for follow-up to roughly Y1 trillion of yen-selling in Asia and Europe so far. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com) [ 09-15-10 1245ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f000ck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
