\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: No Further Evidence Of  \highlight22\uc2 Interventon \highlight\uc2  - Mizhuo\b0\par\par\uc2 1,284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 17:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1505 GMT [Dow Jones] No evidence of direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in U.S. market in the face of emerging scuttle that Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has already acted in N.Y. trading hours, said Hidetoshi Yanagihara, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in New York. Investors are looking for follow-up to roughly Y1 trillion of yen-selling in Asia and Europe so far. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1501 GMT [Dow Jones] The Turkish lira is stronger as EUR gains ground against USD. USD/TRY trades at 1.4905, from 1.4950 Tuesday. Meanwhile bonds are weaker after ratings agency S&P Wednesday reaffirmed that Turkey's sovereign rating is unlikely to be upgraded imminently, even as it revised the country's growth forecast upward and praised its robust economic recovery. The benchmark April 25, 2012 bond ends trades at 8.09% from 8.04% Tuesday and it moves to 8.09% in Thursday value-dated transactions. Analysts forecast TRY will trade between 1.4890 and 1.5010 and the benchmark bond between 8.00% and 8.15%, in the short term. (yeliz.candemir@iha.com.tr)\par \par \uc2 1456 GMT [Dow Jones] The increase in Canadian home sales was mostly in B.C. (up 2.4%) and Ontario (up 5.6%), likely because of a reversal of the decline in sales that coincided with a tax change in both provinces. Home buyers there rushed to buy ahead of the tax implementation to avoid higher financial and legal costs. Canada's existing home sales rose by a seasonally adjusted 0.4% in August, departing from a declining trend that characterized most of this year. Year-over-year, sales were down 22.5%, a marginal improvement from July's 24.9% year-over-year slip. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1452 GMT [Dow Jones] Flows into muni funds continue to be strong, and there's still lots of demand for bond offerings, says Dan Solender at Lord Abbett. For example, a $135M tax-exempt deal Tue for CA's Torrance Memorial Medical Center was oversubscribed at least a couple of times and saw yields lowered, he notes. On Wed, there's lots of offerings in the $50M-$100M range as well as a roughly $639M competitive deal from Washington state as munis prices steady, despite Treasury volatility, Solender says. (kelly.nolan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1449 GMT [Dow Jones] Emerging-market debt swinging between slim gains and losses, in line with mostly flat U.S. equities as market attention remains fixed on the incoming new supply. A string of more corporate bonds, as well as some potential sovereign issues are expected during the rest of the month. Risk premium on \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's Emerging Market Bond Index is 4bps tighter to 309bps over Treasurys; the index slid 0.10% in price terms. Most country components of Embig flat, though Argentine bonds give back some of their gains from the previous session. Brazil's Global 2040 up 1/16 to a bid of 137 3/16. (kejal.vyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1447 GMT [Dow Jones] Hungarian government bond prices rise on a stronger forint. The HUF has been benefiting from the Hungarian government reiterating its 2011 budget deficit goal of less than 3% of gross domestic product. Bond yields are down 7bps-10bps. The 3-year benchmark yield is at 6.78%, 5-year is at 6.82%, 10-year at 6.88%. In the long run, a bond weakening is likely as the government seems adamant that it will not seek IMF support, a trader says. Credit rating downgrades also loom, which would make it hard for Hungary to ensure financing from markets, he adds. EUR/HUF hits 280 earlier in the day, now at 281.60 from 281.73 Tuesday afternoon. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1439 GMT [Dow Jones] In a busy day following \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to beat back the tide of its strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six years, the euro has seen a strong move. With no new data points for the Euro zone, "technical and positioning factors have been important," said \uc2 Wells Fargo\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts. Eurozone consumer price data showed a 0.2% monthly increase to leave prices higher by 1.6% year-over-year, which investors are likely looking to as a recent data marker, pointed out Andrew Wilkinson of Interactive Brokers. EUR/USD, EUR/JPY and EUR/CHF all hit intra-day highs of 1.3029, 111.50 and 1.3062, respectively, one on top of another other in quick succession, according to EBS via CQG. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1440 GMT [Dow Jones] The ruble is being weakened by a number of factors, RBS says. Investors are recognizing that the Russian recovery may be weaker than initially hoped, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap ruble appreciation but is quite happy to see moderate weakness to help growth. In addition, oil has pushed lower over the past 24 hours, while talk that Moscow's powerful mayor could be unseated are adding to an overall negative picture. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1434 GMT [Dow Jones] The market is closely watching the yen, after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets pushed the dollar and the euro sharply higher it. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, if necessary, according to a Kyodo news report. "If you are trying to sell dollar/yen, you have a very limited upside in the near term. You are essentially picking up pennies ahead of the bulldozer," said Firas Askari, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at BMO Capital Markets in Toronto. The dollar and the euro are both up more than 3% vs the yen in late morning in New York. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1428 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds come further off lows after US industrial production data for August narrowly misses forecasts, and the July numbers are revised to show a smaller rise than previously estimated. Core government bonds had opened lower Wednesday after risk sentiment got a slight boost following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities to halt the JPY's rise. However, some traders were still calling for further weakness in bunds, citing selling by certain institutional investors and a weakening technical outlook. "We're likely setting up for a move in the 128.50 area for the December contract, but volatility will remain high," says a London-based dealer. Despite the weak tone in secondary markets, demand was still strong at an EUR5B auction of 10-year bunds. On Thursday, attention will be focussed on an up to EUR4B auction of Spanish bonds, with price concessions likely before the sale. December bunds are down 0.28 at 130.23, and the 10-year bund is down at 98.74 to yield 2.394%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1419 GMT [Dow Jones] Debt continues to flood the market, \uc2 Nissan Motors\uc2  increases ABS to $1.3B from $1B, according to a person familiar with the matter. Auto-maker \uc2 BMW\uc2  has also increased the size of its ABS to $1B from an original $750M and has launched it. Both will price later today.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1419 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro Overnight Index Average fixed higher Tuesday at 0.438% vs 0.422% Monday. "The liquidity situation is still markedly comfortable," a trader says. Wednesday, the interbank overnight rate is trading flat between 0.37% and 0.42%. Earlier Wednesday, 3-month Euribor fixed at 0.876% vs 0.877% Tuesday. (joerg.jaeger@dowjones.com) [ 09-15-10 1105ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f000bm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
