\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Euro Hits Several Intra-Day Highs\b0\par\par\uc2 1,174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 16:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1439 GMT [Dow Jones] In a busy day following \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to beat back the tide of its strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in six years, the euro has seen a strong move. With no new data points for the Euro zone, "technical and positioning factors have been important," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts. Eurozone consumer price data showed a 0.2% monthly increase to leave prices higher by 1.6% year-over-year, which investors are likely looking to as a recent data marker, pointed out Andrew Wilkinson of Interactive Brokers. EUR/USD, EUR/JPY and EUR/CHF all hit intra-day highs of 1.3029, 111.50 and 1.3062, respectively, one on top of another other in quick succession, according to EBS via CQG. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1440 GMT [Dow Jones] The ruble is being weakened by a number of factors, RBS says. Investors are recognizing that the Russian recovery may be weaker than initially hoped, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap ruble appreciation but is quite happy to see moderate weakness to help growth. In addition, oil has pushed lower over the past 24 hours, while talk that Moscow's powerful mayor could be unseated are adding to an overall negative picture. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1434 GMT [Dow Jones] The market is closely watching the yen, after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets pushed the dollar and the euro sharply higher it. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, if necessary, according to a Kyodo news report. "If you are trying to sell dollar/yen, you have a very limited upside in the near term. You are essentially picking up pennies ahead of the bulldozer," said Firas Askari, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at BMO Capital Markets in Toronto. The dollar and the euro are both up more than 3% vs the yen in late morning in New York. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1428 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds come further off lows after US industrial production data for August narrowly misses forecasts, and the July numbers are revised to show a smaller rise than previously estimated. Core government bonds had opened lower Wednesday after risk sentiment got a slight boost following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities to halt the JPY's rise. However, some traders were still calling for further weakness in bunds, citing selling by certain institutional investors and a weakening technical outlook. "We're likely setting up for a move in the 128.50 area for the December contract, but volatility will remain high," says a London-based dealer. Despite the weak tone in secondary markets, demand was still strong at an EUR5B auction of 10-year bunds. On Thursday, attention will be focussed on an up to EUR4B auction of Spanish bonds, with price concessions likely before the sale. December bunds are down 0.28 at 130.23, and the 10-year bund is down at 98.74 to yield 2.394%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1419 GMT [Dow Jones] Debt continues to flood the market, \uc2 Nissan Motors\uc2  increases ABS to $1.3B from $1B, according to a person familiar with the matter. Auto-maker \uc2 BMW\uc2  has also increased the size of its ABS to $1B from an original $750M and has launched it. Both will price later today.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1419 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro Overnight Index Average fixed higher Tuesday at 0.438% vs 0.422% Monday. "The liquidity situation is still markedly comfortable," a trader says. Wednesday, the interbank overnight rate is trading flat between 0.37% and 0.42%. Earlier Wednesday, 3-month Euribor fixed at 0.876% vs 0.877% Tuesday. (joerg.jaeger@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1416 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Universal Health Services\f28 \uc2 \f2  sold $250M in 8-year senior notes at par to yield 7%. The deal, let by \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , will help fund its acquisition of Psychiatric Solutions. The issue was originally slated to be $400M but was cut as some of the financing was moved into the term loans.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (katherine.greene@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1408 GMT [Dow Jones] High-grade corporate issuance is picking up but amounts are still lower than other days this week. In the market: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cliffs Natural Resources\f28 \uc2 \f2  $750M of 10/30-yr notes via BAML and JPM Morgan; JB Hunt $250M 5-yr notes via BAML; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Silicon Valley Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  $350M 10-yr notes via BAML and JPM; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alleghany Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . $300M 10-yr notes via JPM, \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo\f28 \uc2 \f2 . All expected to price Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (michael.aneiro@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1407 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to continue yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thu if necessary, Kyodo News reported. USD/JPY at 85.62, from 83.08 late Tue, according to EBS via CQG. The closely-watched pair has held steady near its intra-day high of 85.78 in U.S. market trading, as investors watch for signs of more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but see no direct evidence thus far. "They sound more aggressive than usual, they usually don't lay out a time-table like this, I think they will be aggressive in the next couple of days, and make a move into other markets," said Mike Moran at Standard Chartered Bank in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1400 GMT [Dow Jones] Mortgage-backed prices are pretty firm after MBA refi index showed a 10% drop in refinancing applications. While magnitude of August prepay report scared investors, it pretty much looks like there just won't be that huge of a paydown wave. And the bulk of the bonds getting hit are in the Fed portfolio. This is actually a good way for the Fed to pare their MBS holdings without major asset sales. (darlele.ross@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1357 GMT [Dow Jones] Fed-funds futures traders price in slightly lower odds for FOMC to begin tightening in 3Q next year. Now seen at 42% chance of hike at next Sept's meeting. That's down from 46% Tues, and 76% last Fri. Move toward reduced rate hike expectations occurs despite release of data showing jump in import prices, calming deflation fears. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1357 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts extend declines, falling in tandem with bunds as stop losses are triggered. Below-par demand at an auction of 20-year gilts, with 1.49x cover, the lowest since July, weighed ahead of a GBP3B auction of 10-year gilts Thursday. "Tuesday's rebound was more of a short squeeze so it was bound to be halted. We opened lower and then [traders in the US] came in and we hit stops along the way," says a London trader. Additionally, monthly UK jobless data showed an unexpected rise. UK retail sales data come Thursday. December gilts down 0.35 at 122.87, 10-year down at 113.664 yielding 3.075%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com) [ 09-15-10 1044ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f000bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
