\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: European Summary\b0\par\par\uc2 1,448 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 14:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1208 GMT [Dow Jones] EUROPEAN SUMMARY: The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday for the first time since March 2006 reportedly spending as much as Y1Tln to halt USD/JPY's slide below Y83.00. The spot immediately added around one yen from its fresh 15-year low of Y82.87 and climbed to a high of 85.54 in Europe while EUR/JPY peaked at a one-month high of 111.11. Dips in USD/JPY were limited to around 85.00 after an MOF official let it be known that further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had taken place during the European session. So far the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been unsterilized, which means it increases money supply and is effectively a form of monetary easing. The BOJ's surprise move helped the dollar recovery elsewhere after Tuesday's sharp sell-off triggered by speculation that the Fed will ease monetary policy again before year end. EUR/USD slipped from 1.3024 to 1.2955, USD/CHF and EUR/CHF added one cent to 1.0049 and 1.3048, respectively, amid speculation that the BOJ's action could trigger a response from the SNB ahead of Thursday rate set meeting. GBP/USD took a small hit after the UK August claimant count unexpectedly rose by 2.3k instead of falling by 4k. However, late session had fully recovered to print the day's high of 1.5569. Elsewhere, gold traded $2 under Tuesday's fresh all-time high of $1274.75oz and the main European bourses are between 0.2% and 0.4% lower. European government bonds are lower with some traders citing the BOJ's unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a factor. December bunds are currently down 0.25 at 130.26 while December gilts are 0.32 lower at 122.90 not helped by a lackluster auction of 20-year gilts. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1207 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY at 85.43, from 83.08 late Tue, on back of first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six years, selling about 1 trillion JPY during Asian and European hours to hinder the yen's appreciation. Investors will be watching closely for any signs of Japan's MOF once US trading become active. Japan prepared to take action again in the US market if needed, a Japanese government official said Wed. EUR/JPY climbs to 110.58 from 108.20, according to EBS via CQG. EUR/USD slightly off at 1.2987 from 1.3020 late Tue, while GBP/USD at 1.5550 from 1.5563. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1155 GMT [Dow Jones] While some of Treasury strength Tues. was attributed to reports there would be another announcement of Fed buying, Richmond Fed Pres Lacker tells WSJ the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should only do more if it was looking at a real threat of consumer price deflation, something he doesn't see. "For me if the growth numbers come in about where the consensus forecast is and we continue to get inflation between 1% and 2%, I don't believe I would see a need for further stimulus. Others may disagree but that's how I see it," Lacker said. Treasurys weak early, despite short end support after yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .(darlene.ross@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/economics/2010/09/14/richmond-feds-lacker-wants-high-threshold-for-more-fed-action/?utm_source=feedburner&utm_medium=feed&utm_campaign=Feed%3A+wsj%2Feconomics%2Ffeed+%28WSJ.com%3A+Real+Time+Economics+Blog%29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/economics/201