\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 :  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Pushes Yen Lower; Investors Anticipate More\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bradley Davis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 14:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The yen was sharply lower Wednesday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in more than six years.\par \par \uc2 After pushing the dollar above Y85, Japanese authorities said they were prepared to extend the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the U.S. session, according to a Japanese government official.\par \par \uc2 After having fallen to a 15-year low Tuesday of Y82.87, the dollar gained more than 2.8% against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Wednesday morning trading in New York to trade at Y85.38 from Y83.08 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 The initial barrage of yen-selling orders hit the market early in the Asian day; it was followed by bursts that pushed the dollar above Y85.\par \par \uc2 The euro, meanwhile, held relatively steady against the dollar, trading at $1.2987 from $1.3020 late Tuesday. The euro shot higher also against the yen, at Y110.80 from Y108.20, while the U.K. pound was at $1.5562 from $1.5563. The dollar was at CHF1.0018 from CHF0.9950.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was up at 81.538 from 81.074.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities continued selling yen into European trading. The government official said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action was partly aimed at countering speculative yen buying.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  about 20 minutes after the first sales hit the market. The wave of yen selling was estimated at Y1 trillion to counter what the government called "severe economic conditions" facing the country.\par \par \uc2 "We conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier to curb excessive fluctuations in exchange rates," Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda told a hastily arranged news conference.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during New York hours, said Steven Englander, head of G10 strategy at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654;\par \par \uc2 bradley.davis@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Takashi Nakamichi and Takashi Mochizuki in Tokyo contributed to this article.) [ 09-15-10 0807ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f0008u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
