 Jones] Treasurys are down in London as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gives risk sentiment a slight boost. It's "a relief that Japanese authorities are drawing a line in the sand and that's feeding into improved risk sentiment," says a strategist. Wednesday data include Empire State Manufacturing Survey at 1230 GMT and industrial production figures at 1315 GMT. The market will look for evidence of a continuation of recent encouraging data. 2-year note down at 99-24/32 yielding 0.504%, 10-year down at 99-11/32 yielding 2.70%. 30-year down at 100-24+/32, yielding 3.832%. December bunds down 0.23 at 130.28. December gilts 0.23 lower at 122.99. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones] The 10-year gilt/bund yield spread edged lower by 1.5 bps to 67 bps after the UK jobless claimant total unexpectedly rose in August. The spread now trades at 67 bps. (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CHF remains in a well defined stair-step downtrend capped by resistance at 1.3165 notes \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . Now at 1.3015 the bank says a break above the 21DMA at 1.3030 would likely see only temporary gains and it would look to sell such a move, looking for a return to the recent lows of 1.2765 and potentially 1.2650. EUR/CHF now at 1.3011. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0838 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP steady late; broad USD strength vs JPY, EUR offering support but continued equity fund inflows, growing overseas workers remittance lift local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Pair at 44.26, trading in narrow 44.11-44.43 band in heavy volume; traders expect USD/PHP to stay in 44.00-44.50 range in near term. "News that tax collection was off target in August may undermine the bullish sentiment for the peso tomorrow," says local bank trader. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0837 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts little moved despite data showing jobless claims rose 2,300 in August vs expectations for a fall by 3,000, continuing recent run of slightly weak data in the UK. December gilts are down 0.20 at 123.03. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0834 GMT [Dow Jones] Sterling dips after the UK jobless claimant total unexpectedly rises in August. GBP/USD sheds around 20 ticks to 1.5495 while EUR/GBP adds 10 ticks to 0.8372. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0826 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex +0.9% at 19,519.08, on course to extend winning streak to 7 sessions as funds buy, with index heavyweights like \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY), +2.4% at INR1,011.20, ONGC (500312.BY), +2.6% at INR1,431, leading gains. "Positive domestic newsflow coupled with sustained foreign inflows have kept the upside momentum intact," says dealer. Adds, strong initial set of July-September corporate advance tax numbers from most sectors and ample liquidity offering support. Says, if Sensex closes above 19,500, may test 19,700 next. Investors expected to keep close eye on RBI policy rate decision due 0630 GMT tomorrow for near-term direction. Maruti (532500.BY) +2.2% at INR1,375.90, \uc2 Infosys (500209.BY) \uc2 +1.6% at INR3,022, Wipro (507685.BY) +2.0% at INR425.60. Among losers, SBI (500112.BY) down 1.2% at INR3,078, \uc2 Tata Motors\uc2  (500570.BY) down 1.7% at INR1,036.40 on weaker-than-expected August sales report. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com) [ 09-15-10 0500ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f0006p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
