\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/JPY Shorts Being "Smoked Out" - Dealer\b0\par\par\uc2 1,111 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 10:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0859 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY may stay around 85.00 rest of global day--at least that's what Japan officials probably want to happen, says senior dealer at major European bank in Tokyo; adds MOF likely has enough firepower to support pair on its own. "I think (Japanese officials) want to end the day by keeping (dollar/yen above) 85.00 because if they could do that, the view would emerge that the pair has hit bottom. That's what they want to happen." Dealer isn't sure if pair may resume fall if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  halts \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; key is if there will be shift in positions as USD "shorts are being smoked out right now." USD/JPY last at 85.45. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0854 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR tad higher at 8,975 vs 8,965 late yesterday as players cover short positions after Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to try to halt JPY's rise vs USD, dealers say; Bank Indonesia not spotted in market today, dealers add. "Capital inflows into Indonesian bond and stock markets put a lid on the greenback," dealer says; 8,965-8,980 range tipped for Thursday. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0852 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/MYR higher late at 3.1130 vs yesterday's 3.1040; local dealer says \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken JPY raising concerns Bank Negara may take additional measures to curb MYR strength. "The pair almost touched MYR3.1000 but reversed direction pretty swiftly after the yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," says dealer. Adds, some corporate demand also driving pair higher, while sellers parked at MYR3.1200 will likely keep resistance level firm today. Market will be closed Thursday for public holiday. Dealer tips 3.1050-3.1250 range Friday. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0844 GMT [Dow Jones] Russian ruble traders are worried as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakens to a four-month low against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-euro basket despite relatively high oil prices this week. "It's quite unpleasant here, looking like short squeeze a bit, local dealers are nervous," says a ruble trader at a major international investment bank in Moscow. Increased imports hurting the trade balance, acquisitions overseas by Russian companies and the maturity of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated debt may be weighing on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trader says. Ruble slips to 34.90 against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket at 0839 GMT, from 34.72 late Tuesday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  little changed at 30.7415 against the dollar. (william.mauldin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0842 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys are down in London as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gives risk sentiment a slight boost. It's "a relief that Japanese authorities are drawing a line in the sand and that's feeding into improved risk sentiment," says a strategist. Wednesday data include Empire State Manufacturing Survey at 1230 GMT and industrial production figures at 1315 GMT. The market will look for evidence of a continuation of recent encouraging data. 2-year note down at 99-24/32 yielding 0.504%, 10-year down at 99-11/32 yielding 2.70%. 30-year down at 100-24+/32, yielding 3.832%. December bunds down 0.23 at 130.28. December gilts 0.23 lower at 122.99. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones] The 10-year gilt/bund yield spread edged lower by 1.5 bps to 67 bps after the UK jobless claimant total unexpectedly rose in August. The spread now trades at 67 bps. (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CHF remains in a well defined stair-step downtrend capped by resistance at 1.3165 notes \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . Now at 1.3015 the bank says a break above the 21DMA at 1.3030 would likely see only temporary gains and it would look to sell such a move, looking for a return to the recent lows of 1.2765 and potentially 1.2650. EUR/CHF now at 1.3011. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0838 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP steady late; broad USD strength vs JPY, EUR offering support but continued equity fund inflows, growing overseas workers remittance lift local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Pair at 44.26, trading in narrow 44.11-44.43 band in heavy volume; traders expect USD/PHP to stay in 44.00-44.50 range in near term. "News that tax collection was off target in August may undermine the bullish sentiment for the peso tomorrow," says local bank trader. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0837 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts little moved despite data showing jobless claims rose 2,300 in August vs expectations for a fall by 3,000, continuing recent run of slightly weak data in the UK. December gilts are down 0.20 at 123.03. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0834 GMT [Dow Jones] Sterling dips after the UK jobless claimant total unexpectedly rises in August. GBP/USD sheds around 20 ticks to 1.5495 while EUR/GBP adds 10 ticks to 0.8372. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0826 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex +0.9% at 19,519.08, on course to extend winning streak to 7 sessions as funds buy, with index heavyweights like \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY), +2.4% at INR1,011.20, ONGC (500312.BY), +2.6% at INR1,431, leading gains. "Positive domestic newsflow coupled with sustained foreign inflows have kept the upside momentum intact," says dealer. Adds, strong initial set of July-September corporate advance tax numbers from most sectors and ample liquidity offering support. Says, if Sensex closes above 19,500, may test 19,700 next. Investors expected to keep close eye on RBI policy rate decision due 0630 GMT tomorrow for near-term direction. Maruti (532500.BY) +2.2% at INR1,375.90, \uc2 Infosys (500209.BY) \uc2 +1.6% at INR3,022, Wipro (507685.BY) +2.0% at INR425.60. Among losers, SBI (500112.BY) down 1.2% at INR3,078, \uc2 Tata Motors\uc2  (500570.BY) down 1.7% at INR1,036.40 on weaker-than-expected August sales report. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0826 GMT [Dow Jones] The EUR/CHF rally faces tough technical resistance at 1.3040 to 1.3070, but thereafter has upside potential to the 1.3150 level, according to \uc2 Zuercher Kantonalbank\uc2 . Support on the downside is seen at 1.2960, with losses below 1.2895 signalling a negative picture, say technical analysts. EUR/CHF at 1.3014. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com) [ 09-15-10 0459ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f0006m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
