w. As \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  notes, there is only "a remote possibility" that the BOC would follow in the BOJ's footsteps and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, BOC Governor Carney did create a stir by pointing to the downside risk that the strength of the CAD poses to the Canadian economy. Bulls will get particularly worried if channel support at CAD1.0111 comes into focus against the USD, the bank says. The USD is now at CAD1.0295. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0737 GMT [Dow Jones] China government bonds end down as PBOC adviser Li Daokui's comment that raising deposit interest rates would benefit China's financial stability renews concerns over possible interest rate hikes. "Concerns over possible tightening measures have hurt the bond market sentiment, spurring heavy selling this afternoon," says Shanghai-based trader with local brokerage. Shanghai exchange government bond index ends at 126.83 vs 126.87 last close, short-term support tipped at 126.75. (ming.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0733 GMT [Dow Jones] There are no signs of any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves by European central banks in agency with the earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  which sold yen versus the dollar for the first time since 2004, according to BayernLB. "There have been no signs of any yen sales by the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 , the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or anybody else in Europe so far today," says trader Roland Raczek. The BOJ is estimated to have sold around $3 billion worth of yen as it tried to check the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation versus the dollar, he adds. USD/JPY at 85.18 having opened the European session at 83.05.(neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0732 GMT [Dow Jones] Don't judge the success of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the size of the move Wednesday. As \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  points out, JPY long positions have been pretty crowded. "The initial reaction has been strong, but is also likely to have been helped by speculative long JPY positions being unwound," the bank says. USD/JPY now at Y85.20, having traded below Y83 earlier. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0729 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are slightly lower ahead of fresh supply Wednesday. Gilts tracked bunds higher Tuesday despite a higher than expected rise in UK core inflation, after the decline in the German ZEW index sparked some concerns over the durability of the economic recovery in the euro zone's largest economy. Attention shifts to unemployment data at 0830 GMT, with BOE Governor King scheduled to speak at 1030 GMT. The DMO also sells GBP2B of 20-year gilts Wednesday, ahead of a GBP3B sale of 10-year gilts on Thursday. December gilts are down 0.10 at 123.12 and the 10-year gilt is down at 113.769 to yield 3.064%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0729 GMT [Dow Jones] Flight-to-quality flows Tuesday supported German bund 2.25% September 2020 and Newedge Strategy says it sees risks of poor demand at Wednesday's EUR5 billion auction as the line looks "quite expensive." However, it adds, that net flows are favorable this week and demand at the auction might be supported by re-investment activity. Separately, \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  says it is "cautious" on the prospects for this auction, given the richness of the bund on offer. Auction results are due at 0900 GMT. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0727 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CHF will trade a tight range around the 1.30 level ahead of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's interest-rate decision Thursday, says BayernLB. "We don't expect any SNB tightening tomorrow, as this will simply make the Swiss franc even more attractive, which the SNB won't want," says trader Roland Raczek. EUR/CHF has support on the downside at 1.2975, and upside resistance at around 1.3050, he adds. EUR/CHF trades at 1.3028. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0726 GMT [Dow Jones] The dampening effect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets had on the yen is set to peter out soon, a strategist says. "I don't think the yen will feel the impact long, much as the franc continues to surge despite previous SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he says. (martin.gelnar@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0726 GMT [Dow Jones] iTraxx Japan Series 13 falls to mid-indication of 96.5 bps vs yesterday's 99 bps as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened JPY, brightening outlook for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key export sector, says Japan bank trader; says, however, tightening move wasn't that large because "players had already had bullish views (over Japan firms), and there's caution ahead of the benchmark index's rollover" later this month. iTraxx actually traded at 99, 98 bps earlier in day. Single-name CDS deals done today include 4-year USD-denominated protection on Japanese sovereign debt at 50 bps vs 49 bps on Monday, \uc2 Sony Corp\uc2 . (6758.TO) at 49 bps vs 56 bps on Sept. 3, \uc2 Komatsu Ltd\uc2 . (6301.TO) at 43 bps. (megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0724 GMT [Dow Jones] September HSI futures down 0.1% at 21,671, mostly in line with cash market's 0.2% decline. Still, throughout session contract trading at small yet consistent premium to cash, now around 10 points, signaling view slight HSI pullback merely normal consolidation as HK market, having risen 9 out of past 10 sessions, may need breather. Volume light at 44,500 lots. (robert.li@dowjones.com) [ 09-15-10 0343ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f0005j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
