\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: MOF  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Is Game Changer - \uc2 TD Securities\b0\par\par\uc2 1,865 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 09:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0704 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's MOF instructs the BOJ to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on its behalf Wednesday, for the first time since March 2004, dragging USD/JPY from below Y83 to an intra-day high of Y85.14. "It is impossible to say how serious the MOF are or at what point they will ease off," says Guillaume Salomon at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 , "but we can at least say that the game has changed and the JPY will now take some time to settle." USD/JPY now at Y84.99. (peter.nurse@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0700 GMT [Dow Jones] The Spanish finance agency is scheduled to sell EUR3 billion 10-year bonds and EUR1 billion 30-year bonds Thursday taking the completed issuance for 2010 to around 72% of the required EUR96 billion, says Nishay Patel, \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  Global Markets strategist. The 10-year bond cheapened versus German bunds Tuesday, with the yield spread widening to 177 bps. This reflects concession building ahead of the auction and Patel fails to see the attraction of the Spanish bonds. "The risk-reward of buying Spain outright or versus Germany looks unattractive to us." (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0655 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may lift its two key policy rates by 25 basis points each at Thursday's monetary policy review in bid to rein in inflationary expectations as economy continues to show robust growth. 10 of 18 economists polled by Dow Jones expect RBI to raise repo, reverse repo rate by 25 bps, while four expect 25 bps hike in only reverse repo. "The economy is on a roll, clearly, but so are price pressures. This requires a determined tap on the brake by policy-makers. Rates need to go higher still," \uc2 HSBC\uc2  economist Frederic Neumann says. India's August inflation 9.5% on-year, slower than July 9.97%, below 9.6% estimated in Dow Jones poll, as per old series. Factory output for July +13.8%, well-above estimated 7.8%. Decision due 0630 GMT Thursday. (subhadip.sircar@dowjones.com, khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0648 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore stocks generally still firm, with small caps continuing to lead gains. Market breadth at 2 gainers for every decliner. "Blue chips are being sidelined as traders zoom in on small caps and S-chips. There's a fair bit of momentum in the market," says dealer at foreign brokerage. FTSE ST Small Cap Index +0.9%, FTSE ST China Index +0.9% vs STI +0.4% at 3062.06. If year-to-date high of 3068 gives way, next resistance for STI expected at lower end of 3085-3146 breakdown gap formed in June 2008. Notable gainers among small caps, S-chips include \uc2 China Hongxing Sports\uc2  (BR9.SG), +7.5% at S$0.215, Yangzijiang (BS6.SG), +4.8% at S$1.75, Cosco (F83.SG), +3.1% at S$1.68, Informatics (I03.SG), +6.1% at S$0.175. Among blue chips, developers underperforming after fresh official data released during midday break showed developers sold fewer homes in August, 1,248 vs 1,549 in July. \uc2 CapitaLand\uc2  (C31.SG) off 0.5% at S$4.00, CityDev (C09.SG) flat at S$11.62. (frankie.ho@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0648 GMT [Dow Jones] China onshore IRS down, snapping 3-day winning streak, after U.S. treasury yields fall significantly. 1-year down 1 bp at 2.10%-2.17%, 5-year down 1 bp at 2.81%-2.88%. "Recent gains aren't sustainable as I see most traders are just taking profit on their long positions," says Shanghai-based foreign bank trader. IRS up around 10 bps in past 3 days on robust August China economic data. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0647 GMT [Dow Jones] BOJ policy board member Noda says BOJ will continue to provide ample funds into financial markets, also considering to making use of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds; comment suggests that BOJ may not soak up extra \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from market, leave \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "unsterilized". If that's true, it'll strengthen BOJ's already-accommodative monetary policy even further and help show \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's easing stance more clearly to market players. Noda adds, funds that entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "have a temporary ability to provide money to the financial market." (megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0646 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian government bonds' prices surge in moderate volume as foreign funds enter market after week-long holiday, dealers say. "In general, appetite for high-yielding assets in emerging markets is on the rise. The big jump for the bonds is simply because our market was closed during Eid holidays," dealer at local securities firm says; adds downward correction for short-dated bond likely in 4Q due to high inflation. Elsewhere foreigners buy IDR1.5 trillion ($168 million) worth of stocks. 5-year yield drops to 7.38% vs 7.59% on Sep. 7, before market's break; 10-year at 7.93% vs 8.13%; 15-year at 8.49% vs 8.72%; 20-year at 8.98% vs 9.20%. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0643 GMT [Dow Jones] HSI down 0.1% at 21,677.60, on mild profit-taking after index gained 9 out of past 10 sessions; volume solid at HK$40.22 billion. Still, pullback looks like normal consolidation; in view of current market sentiment, volume, HSI Index may next test early August high of 21,800, says South China Research, though adds that slew of fund-raising activities may "put off some investors." Blue chips largely in consolidation mode: only 3 stocks rising or falling more than 2%; \uc2 China Resources Enterprise\uc2  (0291.HK) down 3.1% at HK$32.50, succumbing to profit-taking after setting 52-week high yesterday, is worst-performing index member. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0642 GMT [Dow Jones] The DMO auctions GBP2 Bln UKT 2030 Wednesday, ahead of a GBP3 Bln auction of 10-year gilts Thursday, and the timing could leave the sale susceptible, says Nomura. "The prevailing steepness in the curve, despite fundamentals, suggests that the gilt market may be struggling to fully digest the supply that has come before it despite what looks to be a lighter burden for the remainder of the fiscal year," Nomura says, noting the recent decline in bid-to-cover ratios at auctions. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0634 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds are down Wednesday, with European equities set to open up tracking their Asian peers. Stocks in Asia were generally higher, led by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  where equities rose after authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to try to halt the JPY's rise. The market is also preparing for supply, with an EUR5B bund auction lined up later in the session. The data calendar sees euro-zone harmonized CPI and employment data at 0900 GMT, while in the US, the Empire State Index and industrial production figures are due at 1230 GMT and 1315 GMT, respectively. "With the manufacturing survey carrying more forward-looking information the macro support for bond markets should remain in place, especially as euro-zone core inflation is forecast to slip below 1% again," says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . December bunds are down 0.11 at 130.40 and the 10-year bund is down at 98.84 to yield 2.383%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0630 GMT [Dow Jones] India's inflation likely to moderate further on drop in primary product prices due to good monsoon, favorable base effect, says Citi in report. India from Tuesday moved to FY05 as base year for calculating inflation from earlier FY94 and introduced new wholesale price index series including 676 items vs 435 earlier. August inflation print based on new index came in at 8.5% vs 9.8% in July. House revises expectations of average inflation in FY11 to 7.9% vs 8.8% earlier to adjust for new WPI series and new base year. It however, expects RBI to hike both repo, reverse repo rates by 25 bps on Thursday given macro trends in non-food credit, tax collections and sectoral data on autos, cement, diesel etc. House notes RBI saying that policy rates are still "far from a normal position." (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0627 GMT [Dow Jones] ASIAN SUMMARY: Regional markets mixed; Nikkei sharply up on JPY selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities; Nikkei Stock Average +2.3% at 9516.56 vs intraday low of 9199.08. S&P/ASX 200 +0.7%, Kospi +0.5%, Shanghai Composite off 0.6%, HSI +0.1%, Taiex +0.4%, STI +0.5%, KLCI down 0.3%, SET down 1.3%, NZX-50 off 0.1%; Indonesia +3.8% in catch-up after holidays there. \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets roiled by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for first time in over 6 years with wave of JPY selling to deal with "severe economic conditions" facing country. USD/JPY at 84.88 (earlier hit 85.08) vs 83.08 late NY Tuesday, off new 15-year low of 82.87 before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . EUR/USD at 1.2991 vs 1.3020 in late NY trade Tuesday, EUR/JPY at 110.26 vs 108.20. Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weaken in tandem with JPY; players fear Asian central banks' could follow \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lead. "We conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier to curb excessive fluctuations in exchange rates. We will continue to closely monitor movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will take decisive steps, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when necessary," \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda says in news conference. \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if USD/SGD falls below 1.3300, says person familiar \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking; USD/SGD last at 1.3366. Mixed Australia data: index of consumer sentiment fell 5% on-month in September to 113.2 points seasonally adjusted vs 119.2 August, say \uc2 Westpac Banking Corp\uc2 ., Melbourne Institute; 2Q total house, apartment starts +0.8% on-quarter to seasonally adjusted 44,899; worse than +3.0% forecast. But index of job vacancies for skilled workers +0.1% on-month in September, 16% higher so far on the year. South Korea August jobless rate at 3.4% seasonally adjusted, down from 3.7% in July; country's August exports +27.7% on-year revised at $36.97 billion, imports +28.6% on-year revised at $35.25 billion, trade surplus revised to $1.72 billion vs $2.08 billion. China August FDI at $7.6 billion, +1.38% on-year; compares with $6.92 billion in July, +29.2% on-year, rapid deceleration from June's +39.6%. Singapore unemployment rate unchanged at 2.2% in 2Q vs 1Q. Spot gold at $1,268.70 per troy ounce, flat vs New York Tuesday. October crude oil futures down 55 cents at $76.25/bbl. (matthew.allen@dowjones.com) [ 09-15-10 0304ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f0004t\par }\page {\