\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Timing Could Leave UK 2030 Gilt Sale Susceptible\b0\par\par\uc2 1,796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 08:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0642 GMT [Dow Jones] The DMO auctions GBP2 Bln UKT 2030 Wednesday, ahead of a GBP3 Bln auction of 10-year gilts Thursday, and the timing could leave the sale susceptible, says Nomura. "The prevailing steepness in the curve, despite fundamentals, suggests that the gilt market may be struggling to fully digest the supply that has come before it despite what looks to be a lighter burden for the remainder of the fiscal year," Nomura says, noting the recent decline in bid-to-cover ratios at auctions. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0634 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds are down Wednesday, with European equities set to open up tracking their Asian peers. Stocks in Asia were generally higher, led by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  where equities rose after authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to try to halt the JPY's rise. The market is also preparing for supply, with an EUR5B bund auction lined up later in the session. The data calendar sees euro-zone harmonized CPI and employment data at 0900 GMT, while in the US, the Empire State Index and industrial production figures are due at 1230 GMT and 1315 GMT, respectively. "With the manufacturing survey carrying more forward-looking information the macro support for bond markets should remain in place, especially as euro-zone core inflation is forecast to slip below 1% again," says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . December bunds are down 0.11 at 130.40 and the 10-year bund is down at 98.84 to yield 2.383%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0630 GMT [Dow Jones] India's inflation likely to moderate further on drop in primary product prices due to good monsoon, favorable base effect, says Citi in report. India from Tuesday moved to FY05 as base year for calculating inflation from earlier FY94 and introduced new wholesale price index series including 676 items vs 435 earlier. August inflation print based on new index came in at 8.5% vs 9.8% in July. House revises expectations of average inflation in FY11 to 7.9% vs 8.8% earlier to adjust for new WPI series and new base year. It however, expects RBI to hike both repo, reverse repo rates by 25 bps on Thursday given macro trends in non-food credit, tax collections and sectoral data on autos, cement, diesel etc. House notes RBI saying that policy rates are still "far from a normal position." (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0627 GMT [Dow Jones] ASIAN SUMMARY: Regional markets mixed; Nikkei sharply up on JPY selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities; Nikkei Stock Average +2.3% at 9516.56 vs intraday low of 9199.08. S&P/ASX 200 +0.7%, Kospi +0.5%, Shanghai Composite off 0.6%, HSI +0.1%, Taiex +0.4%, STI +0.5%, KLCI down 0.3%, SET down 1.3%, NZX-50 off 0.1%; Indonesia +3.8% in catch-up after holidays there. \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets roiled by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for first time in over 6 years with wave of JPY selling to deal with "severe economic conditions" facing country. USD/JPY at 84.88 (earlier hit 85.08) vs 83.08 late NY Tuesday, off new 15-year low of 82.87 before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . EUR/USD at 1.2991 vs 1.3020 in late NY trade Tuesday, EUR/JPY at 110.26 vs 108.20. Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weaken in tandem with JPY; players fear Asian central banks' could follow \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lead. "We conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier to curb excessive fluctuations in exchange rates. We will continue to closely monitor movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will take decisive steps, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when necessary," \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda says in news conference. \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if USD/SGD falls below 1.3300, says person familiar \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking; USD/SGD last at 1.3366. Mixed Australia data: index of consumer sentiment fell 5% on-month in September to 113.2 points seasonally adjusted vs 119.2 August, say \uc2 Westpac Banking Corp\uc2 ., Melbourne Institute; 2Q total house, apartment starts +0.8% on-quarter to seasonally adjusted 44,899; worse than +3.0% forecast. But index of job vacancies for skilled workers +0.1% on-month in September, 16% higher so far on the year. South Korea August jobless rate at 3.4% seasonally adjusted, down from 3.7% in July; country's August exports +27.7% on-year revised at $36.97 billion, imports +28.6% on-year revised at $35.25 billion, trade surplus revised to $1.72 billion vs $2.08 billion. China August FDI at $7.6 billion, +1.38% on-year; compares with $6.92 billion in July, +29.2% on-year, rapid deceleration from June's +39.6%. Singapore unemployment rate unchanged at 2.2% in 2Q vs 1Q. Spot gold at $1,268.70 per troy ounce, flat vs New York Tuesday. October crude oil futures down 55 cents at $76.25/bbl. (matthew.allen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0618 GMT [Dow Jones] HK short-selling volume down 1.4% at HK$1.406 billion at interval, 3.7% of market total, staying low vs 3.8% Tuesday's half-day, suggesting HSI may remain rangebound after recent gains (+0.05% midday). China National Building Material (3323.HK) leads with HK$117.94 million, \uc2 Hutchison Whampoa\uc2  (0013.HK) with HK$82.26 million, Agricultural Bank of China (1288.HK) with HK$71.50 million, Anhui Conch (0914.HK) with HK$53.22 million and \uc2 Sun Hung Kai Properties\uc2  (0016.HK) with HK$48.87 million. (susanna.tai@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0617 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since 1Q 2004, to try and stem the yen's recent rise. USD/JPY stands at Y84.81, from Y83.03 in NY trading late Tuesday. "Although the overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should put a short term floor under USD/JPY, we expect the pair to remain heavy over the medium term as the market continues to worry about the possibility of further quantitative easing by the Fed," says \uc2 UBS\uc2 . (peter.nurse@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0615 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday, pushing USD/JPY initially above Y85 and EUR/JPY above Y110. "It has yet to be seen if it will be successful or not, but the speculative market is long the yen," says SEB. "A high EUR/JPY, USD/JPY close today will indicate that it will likely take a few days before the market is testing the MOF's intentions again." USD/JPY stands at Y84.81, from Y83.03 in NY trading late Tuesday, and EUR/JPY at Y110.22, from Y107.96.(peter.nurse@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0612 GMT [Dow Jones] December bunds are 0.10 lower at 130.41, slipping after posting robust gains on Tuesday. \uc2 DZ Bank\uc2  says it prefers to play the contract from the short side while the 2-week downward trend remains intact, with trading expected to be volatile. Support is at 130.05 and 129.53. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0608 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan shares end +0.4% at 8163.82 with touch panel stocks leading gains; but profit-taking pressure mounting after benchmark index gained 4.2% in past 4 sessions, says Grand Cathay Securities analyst Mars Hsu. "Room for further gains is limited. 8200 will be the key resistance in the near term." Tips Taiex in tight 8110-8200 range Thursday. Adds, touch panel makers draw decent buying interest as touch screen gadgets have been well-received by market. Wintek (2384.NT) +7.0% at NT$49.15 but HTC (2498.TW) down 3.3% at NT$730.00 on profit-taking after having gained 17% in last 4 sessions. (lorraine.luk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0606 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares off 1.3% at 909.76 at midday pause in active trade. Across-the-board fall weighed by worries whether \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  may impose measures to curb baht rise; sudden gains in USD/THB on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to dealers, in wake of Tokyo's JPY \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also prompting investors to lock in profit, says Phillip Securities' assistant vice president Teerada Chanyingyong. Benchmark briefly hit 2-week-low of 902.46 intrasession before bargain hunting kicked, trimmed losses. "The index slipping through 915 support for today caused some short-term negative sentiment. If 900 psychological support cannot hold, this may lead to a big downward correction," Teerada says. Notes eyes on court's hearing today on legal challenge to 3G mobile license auction, with state-owned \uc2 CAT Telecom\uc2  seeking injunction. Resistance at 912. Among top actives, PTT (PTT.TH) down 1.4% at THB278, \uc2 Kasikornbank\uc2  (KBANK.TH) down 2.8% at THB104.50, \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2  (SCB.TH) down 3.4% at THB91.25, Banpu (BANPU.TH) down 0.6% at THB632. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0605 GMT [Dow Jones] Australia's Bureau of Meteorology points out that current La Nina event in Pacific Basin, which usually associated with average to above average rainfall in eastern, northern Australia, coincides with negative Indian Ocean Dipole, which is usually associated with average to above average rainfall in southern Australia. Combination of both climatic events suggest winter crops in eastern Australia, including wheat and barley, could be in for a wet spring and possibly a wet harvest in November, December. If this comes to pass, quality of winter crops could be downgraded, such as through staining, or lower protein content for wheat, and so command a lower price on market. The Australian Oilseeds Federation reported today that in New South Wales and Victoria there is already sufficient soil moisture in most regions to carry the crop through to harvest, which suggest that these crops prone to damage if further heavy falls occur. (ray.brindal@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0604 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weren't the only place affected by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with Australian bonds falling on both ends of curve as well. "It did pressure our market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted Nikkei strength and broader Asian equity market rallies and that put some pressure on Aussie 3-years," says Sydney-based bond trader; reckons more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could mean more bond weakness. Aussie 3-year bonds recently off 3 ticks at 95.235. Also on session, Aussie bond contracts rolled over from September to December, though traders say MOF moves overshadowed roll over. (geoffrey.rogow@dowjones.com) [ 09-15-10 0242ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f0004j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwg