et rate," he points out. EUR/CHF at 1.3005. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0557 GMT [Dow Jones] Today's rallying AUD/JPY on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be end of gains for pair, says Kurt Magnus, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Nomura in Sydney. "With these type of actions, it give confidence in central banks trying to reflate global economies. This won't be a 24-hour phenomenon," says Magnus. AUD/JPY up to 79.595 recently from around 77.95 just prior to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  news, marking highest point since early August. AUD/USD should also be strong, says Magnus; adds, "there is every reason to continue buying Aussie, not just because of yield and carry advantage, but also because of the implications of an Asian-led growth story that has fed directly into commodities, especially gold and precious metals." AUD/USD recently at 0.9378 after reaching new two-year high of 0.9457 overnight. (geoffrey.rogow@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0557 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/KRW trims gains on export settlements, foreign equity fund inflows, traders say. Pair last at 1,162.3 vs 1,166.5 earlier high, but likely to remain above 1,161.7 late yesterday in Seoul due to expected corporate demand related to recent M&A deals. Players also remain wary of possible BOK \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (to support pair) following \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier to weaken JPY. Local bank trader expects USD/KRW to consolidate around current levels for rest of session. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0541 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian shares +3.8% at 3353.537 midday in heavy volume as foreign investors buy after week-long holiday, dealers say. "Sentiment is positive but gains will likely be limited in the afternoon session," dealer says. Foreigners net buyers in local bourse today, picking up about IDR1.5 trillion ($168 million) worth of shares. Among gainers, \uc2 Astra International\uc2  (ASII.JK) +8.9% at IDR58,250; Telkom (TLKM.JK) +4.4% at IDR9,400; \uc2 Bank Mandiri\uc2  (BMRI.JK) +9.5% at IDR6,900 after \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  raised its target price; \uc2 Indofood\uc2  (INDF.JK) +7.7% at IDR5,250; Bumi (BUMI.JK) +5.2% at IDR1,810. 3,300-3,380 band tipped for rest of session.(andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0540 GMT [Dow Jones] India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to take a rate action on Thursday even though August inflation, as per new wholesale price index series, shows larger-than-expected fall, says \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 . "Inflationary expectations are likely to be still relatively elevated since in level terms food prices are yet to see a notable correction," says house. Adds, consumer faces higher fuel prices across the board, from price hikes implemented in July. House expects base case 25 bp hike in only reverse repo rate but does not rule out hike in repo rate. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0540 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: Hong Kong's jobless rate likely held steady at 4.3% in June-August period, according to median forecast of 10 economists polled by Dow Jones. Still, economists say it could fall toward year-end as city's economy continues to grow. "Domestic demand remains robust due to the strength of the local economy, and the situation surrounding Europe's sovereign debt crisis is better-than-expected, which helped to support Hong Kong's labor market," says \uc2 Bank of East Asia\uc2  economist Paul Tang. Tips jobless rate to fall to 4.0% by year-end. Data due 0830 GMT Thursday. (chester.yung@dowjones.com) [ 09-15-10 0215ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f00049\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
