to median forecast of 10 economists polled by Dow Jones. Still, economists say it could fall toward year-end as city's economy continues to grow. "Domestic demand remains robust due to the strength of the local economy, and the situation surrounding Europe's sovereign debt crisis is better-than-expected, which helped to support Hong Kong's labor market," says \uc2 Bank of East Asia\uc2  economist Paul Tang. Tips jobless rate to fall to 4.0% by year-end. Data due 0830 GMT Thursday. (chester.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0530 GMT [Dow Jones] After 6-year absence, Japan's MOF has returned to \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell JPY; this time BOJ is cooperating by not sterilizing the surplus liquidity. However, Japan is taking on largest 24-hour market in world so success may be measured on more modest scale than in previous battles. Wherever USD/JPY is heading from here, next 24 hours may be crucial in changing psychology of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders. See: =MONEY TALKS: Japan Takes On The $4 Trillion Monster (mark.cranfield@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0527 GMT [Dow Jones] Tokyo Stock Exchange (TSE) President Atsushi Saito welcomes \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  government's decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. "What is the most important thing for Japan now is to have a decisive stance and show \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators that measures can be taken to counter the unnatural state of the yen's rise." Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is merely "symptomatic therapy" (measure to treat symptoms, not cause) for deflation, hopes Kan administration to come up with solid growth strategy to counter Japan's ongoing deflationary problem. Nikkei up 2.8%, USD/JPY at 84.99. (ayai.tomisawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0520 GMT [Dow Jones] After 6-year absence Japan's MOF has returned to \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell JPY; this time BOJ is cooperating by not sterilizing the surplus liquidity. However, Japan is taking on largest 24-hour market in world so success may be measured on more modest scale than in previous battles. Wherever USD/JPY is heading from here, next 24 hours may be crucial in changing psychology of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders. (mark.cranfield@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0519 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan government bonds up, tracking rally in U.S. Treasurys overnight, while investors turn cautious as they try to figure out how \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will affect TWD, and overall domestic economy, says trader from local brokerage. Adds, bonds unlikely to rise sharply with no strong lead from local stock market to help affirm clear direction. Still, "the economic outlook is not great so the new 10-year bond yield should remain low." Tips 1.20%-1.25% range at 10-year bond auction tomorrow. 10-year yield last at 1.2260% vs 1.2401% yesterday, tipped in 1.21%-1.23% Thursday. 5-year yield last at 0.8850% vs 0.8860%. (paul.mozur@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0518 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD steady after drifting off all day from overnight high of 0.7396; "It seems to be stabilizing at the moment, and I think it is probably still a buy on dips, but you may get support around 0.7270 and that may be a bit of an opportunity," says \uc2 HSBC\uc2  NZ Chief Manager Daniel Brdanovic. Pair last at 0.7321. Says NZD, AUS, EUR likely to find further support after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on USD/JPY earlier and "it seems to be a risk on environment at the moment." Tips initial resistance at overnight high. Says market expecting RBNZ to remain on hold at tomorrow's rate review and while may be dovish on econo